  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 216 PM MDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nThursday night through Monday: Monsoonal moisture retreats out \nof our County Warning Area (CWA) as a drier and hotter air mass \nreturns producing nearly dry conditions with only minimal \nchances for isolated to scattered thunderstorms over and near \nour Snowy, Sierra Madre, and Laramie Ranges due to differential \norographic processes. Temperatures will soar once again, \nespecially for Sunday and Monday, with some locations possibly \napproaching near record maximum temperatures, and perhaps the \nlong standing all time record high temperature of 100 degrees at\nCheyenne, that has been achieved four times, the most recent in\nthe 1950s.",
